<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
     <VersionPrefix>1.5.0</VersionPrefix>
     
      <PackageReleaseNotes>
          - On .NET 11, you can validate files and directories with PathUtil.GetFileResult, GetFilesResult, GetDirectoryResult, and GetDirectoriesResult and handle validation failures as values rather than exceptions. When you validate a batch, you get all the resolved paths in order or one error listing every failure, with no partial results.
          - On .NET 11, you can use the Result unions to represent success or failure and chain steps with Bind, BindToMatchAsync, or BindToValueAsync. If a step returns an error, you get that error back unchanged.
          - On .NET 11, you can use PathOrError as a typed result through implicit conversion. You can still use the exception-based TryGet helpers on both .NET 10 and .NET 11.
      </PackageReleaseNotes>
       <TargetFrameworks>net11.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
       <LangVersion Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net11.0'">15.0</LangVersion>
      <LangVersion Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' != 'net11.0'">14.0</LangVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
